
'v8_in_unity' is the Unity native plugin that allows our Unity code (such as
VoosEngine) to use V8, Chromium's JavaScript engine. It provides functions for
compiling scripts at run time, interacting between JS and the actor model, etc.

The wrapper source, ABI header, and native regression harness live here. The
V8 engine source and its dependencies are fetched from upstream at the pinned
revision documented in [`BUILDING.md`](BUILDING.md). The Windows build script
generates and tests the x64 native plugin before installing it in Unity assets.

The historical V8 pin is `d2e0166ded485df126c765b9196f7edd1ce50f82`
(V8 7.1.0.0). Both Visual Studio and Xcode projects take local V8 paths as
`V8_ROOT`/`V8_OUT`; no developer-specific absolute paths are required.